Space Invaders implementation — design rationale & decisions

WHY this approach
- Engine is pure TypeScript (no React) so it is unit-testable and portable;
  React only appears in the thin GameIsland wrapper that binds engine
  start()/destroy() to component mount/unmount (prevents RAF + key-listener
  leaks across HMR/navigation).
- Updates are delta-time based (px/second), with the loop clamping dt to
  0.05s. This makes motion identical at 30/60/144Hz and prevents a huge
  position jump after the tab is backgrounded.
- Bullet uses the SIGN of its speed as its direction (no subclass / flag):
  negative = player (up), positive = alien (down). One class, two roles.
- AlienGrid owns all movement so the swarm marches in lock-step and reverses
  + descends the instant ANY living alien touches an edge (apply-then-correct
  overflow keeps it on-canvas at both edges). March speed scales with kills to
  mirror the arcade's rising tension. Only the frontmost alien per column may
  fire (can't shoot through the one below).
- InputHandler keeps a held-key Set for per-frame polling, plus an
  edge-triggered consumeStart() so a single Space press starts/restarts
  without auto-repeat skipping screens.
- Player.shoot() is cooldown rate-limited so holding Space can't emit a bullet
  every frame; dead bullets are pruned each frame to avoid unbounded growth.

TESTING — why it matters
- Canvas pixels are opaque to unit tests, so vitest targets pure logic: bounds
  clamping, off-screen bullet pruning (memory-leak guard), swarm reversal/
  descent, bottom-of-column firing, and the SpaceInvaders state machine
  (start->playing->won/gameover->restart) via a stubbed 2D context. E2E
  (Playwright) covers the visual/integration gap: canvas mounts at 800x600,
  input raises no console errors, and the canvas pixels change when the game
  starts.

GOTCHAS recorded for future loops
- Run Playwright with --reporter=list in agent/CI shells; the default html
  reporter opens a blocking report server (caused an initial hang).
- npx playwright install chromium is required once in a fresh environment.
- vite build (emptyOutDir) wipes src/app/static and removes .gitkeep; restore
  it. Built assets are gitignored.
- ESLint flat config lacks DOM type globals -> avoid `as EventListener` casts;
  type handlers as (e: Event) and narrow.
- Pre-commit mypy/flake8 pass explicit filenames, bypassing the migrations
  exclude in pyproject/setup.cfg; added matching `exclude: ^migrations/` to the
  hooks (single source of truth: project already excludes migrations).
- Strict mypy: test client param typed `FlaskClient[Any]` needs
  `from __future__ import annotations` so the subscript isn't evaluated at
  runtime (FlaskClient isn't subscriptable at runtime).
